# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC, AND IT IS ALSO THE LIVE WEBSITE.
#
# Anything committed here is downloadable by anyone, twice over: from
# learnactively.com and straight from github.com with no account. Measured
# 2026-11-10: an anonymous request for a chapter of the author's book returned
# HTTP 200 and 31,985 bytes.
#
# So what belongs here is what a learner's browser needs, and nothing else.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE AUTHORS' BOOKS. Not negotiable.
#
# cma/book*/assets/source-text*.js is each CMA volume EXTRACTED VERBATIM from
# the author's .docx - 405,754 words across the four volumes, every file headed
# with the name and sha256 of the source document. No learner page loads them.
# They exist because the provenance lock checks the site's every word against
# the book, and five readers need them ON DISK: gates/cma_provenance,
# gates/cma_coverage, gates/cma_shared, tools/cma_book and tools/cma_extract_all.
#
# Ignoring rather than deleting is the whole point: the files stay exactly where
# those five expect them, and leave the public repository and the website. They
# are regenerable with `python -m tools.cma_book --book N --chapter C --baseline`
# from the .docx in D:\____All_Books, so a fresh clone that lacks them is a few
# minutes of work, not a loss.
cma/book*/assets/source-text*.js

# The internal quality-gate pages. They are a harness, driven by
# gates/cma_render through a local server; they load the baselines above, so
# publishing them without those would serve a broken page to nobody's benefit.
cma/book*/_qa*.html

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working documents. These were committed here once and were public until
# 2026-11-10; they now live in Apps\_internal_packages\. A path has to be
# NAMED to travel - see each course's tools/publish.py whitelist.
*.docx
*.doc
*.zip
*.log
cma/book*/plan_*/
cma/book*/build_*/
cma/book*/delivered_*/
cma/book*/source/

# Editor and tool droppings
.playwright-mcp/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
